### Rate Limiting

The daemon tracks rate limits per executable and pauses dispatch when limits are detected.

#### handleRateLimitDetected

Notify the daemon that a rate limit was detected for an executable. Called externally (e.g., from event listeners on session events). The daemon pauses dispatching for the affected executable until the reset time.

```typescript
handleRateLimitDetected(executable: string, resetsAt: Date): void
```

```typescript
daemon.handleRateLimitDetected('claude', new Date(Date.now() + 3600000));
```

#### getRateLimitStatus

Returns the current rate limit status for the daemon.

```typescript
getRateLimitStatus(): {
  isPaused: boolean;
  limits: Array<{ executable: string; resetsAt: string }>;
  soonestReset?: string;
}
```

```typescript
const status = daemon.getRateLimitStatus();
if (status.isPaused) {
  console.log(`Rate limited until ${status.soonestReset}`);
  for (const limit of status.limits) {
    console.log(`  ${limit.executable} resets at ${limit.resetsAt}`);
  }
}
```

#### sleepUntil

Manually put the daemon to sleep until the specified time. Marks all executables in the fallback chain as rate-limited until the given time. Reuses the existing rate limit tracker and pause logic.

```typescript
