## Bug Fix: Notion rejects text blocks longer than 2000 characters

**Problem:** When syncing documents to Notion, POST /pages fails with:
"body.children[N].paragraph.rich_text[0].text.content.length should be ≤ 2000, instead was XXXX"

Notion limits each rich_text element's text.content to 2000 characters. Our markdownToNotionBlocks() converter creates one rich_text element per paragraph with no length check.

### Fix

**Location:** packages/quarry/src/external-sync/providers/notion/notion-blocks.ts, markdownToNotionBlocks()

When generating any block that contains rich_text (paragraph, heading, quote, bulleted_list_item, numbered_list_item, to_do), split text content that exceeds 2000 characters into multiple rich_text elements within the same block. Each rich_text element should be at most 2000 characters, splitting at word boundaries when possible.

```typescript
function chunkRichText(text: string, maxLength = 2000): NotionRichText[] {
  if (text.length <= maxLength) {
    return [{ type: 'text', text: { content: text } }];
  }
  const chunks: NotionRichText[] = [];
  let remaining = text;
  while (remaining.length > 0) {
    if (remaining.length <= maxLength) {
      chunks.push({ type: 'text', text: { content: remaining } });
      break;
    }
    // Split at last space before maxLength
    let splitAt = remaining.lastIndexOf(' ', maxLength);
    if (splitAt <= 0) splitAt = maxLength; // No space found, hard split
    chunks.push({ type: 'text', text: { content: remaining.slice(0, splitAt) } });
    remaining = remaining.slice(splitAt).trimStart();
  }
  return chunks;
}
```

Apply this to ALL block types that contain rich_text. Preserve formatting annotations (bold, italic, code, link) across chunks — if a chunk splits in the middle of a formatted span, the annotation should carry over to the next chunk.

Also apply to code blocks: Notion's code block content has the same 2000-char limit. Split long code blocks into multiple consecutive code blocks with the same language annotation.

