## Problem

When the daemon is rate-limited, worker sessions exit rapidly and burn through the `resumeCount` budget (hitting `maxResumeAttemptsBeforeRecovery`). After the user presses "Wake Now", the daemon tries to recover orphaned tasks but sees `resumeCount >= maxResumes` (line ~1187 in `dispatch-daemon.ts`) and routes them to the recovery steward instead of resuming the worker normally.

This is wrong — the resume budget was consumed by rate-limit-induced failures, not by the worker being genuinely stuck. After wake, the worker should get a fresh chance.

## Principle

Same as el-5c9f: `wake()` must invalidate all stale rate-limit-era state. `resumeCount` is another input that was inflated during the rate limit period and should not penalize the worker after wake.

## Fix

In the orphan recovery loop (~line 1182-1187), use the existing `lastWakeAt` timestamp (added in el-5c9f) to detect tasks whose last session predates the wake. If so, reset `resumeCount` to 0 before checking the threshold.

```typescript
// ~line 1182, before checking resumeCount >= maxResumes:
const taskAssignment = workerTasks[0];
let resumeCount = taskAssignment.orchestratorMeta?.resumeCount ?? 0;
const maxResumes = this.config.maxResumeAttemptsBeforeRecovery;

// Reset resume budget if the task's last activity predates a manual wake.
// Rate-limited sessions burn through resumeCount without the worker being
// genuinely stuck — give it a fresh start after wake.
if (this.lastWakeAt && resumeCount >= maxResumes) {
  const lastSessionStart = this.getLastSessionStartTime(taskAssignment.orchestratorMeta);
  if (lastSessionStart && lastSessionStart < this.lastWakeAt) {
    logger.info(
      `Resetting resumeCount for task ${taskAssignment.task.id} (was ${resumeCount}) — ` +
      `last session predates manual wake`
    );
    resumeCount = 0;
    // Persist the reset so it doesn't keep triggering
    await this.api.update(taskAssignment.task.id, {
      metadata: updateOrchestratorTaskMeta(
        taskAssignment.task.metadata as Record<string, unknown> | undefined,
        { resumeCount: 0 }
      ),
    });
  }
}
```

Add a small helper to extract the last session start time from task metadata:

```typescript
private getLastSessionStartTime(
  taskMeta: OrchestratorTaskMeta | undefined
): number | undefined {
  const history = taskMeta?.sessionHistory;
  if (!history || history.length === 0) return undefined;
  return new Date(history[history.length - 1].startedAt).getTime();
}
```

