Problem: When creating an OpenCode headless session, the error "OpenCode session creation failed: no session ID returned" is thrown without surfacing the actual server error. In packages/smithy/src/providers/opencode/headless.ts (line 196-202), the code checks result.data?.id but never inspects result.error. The OpenCode SDK client returns { error, request, response } (no data field) for non-200 responses, so any server-side error is silently lost.

Additionally, newer OpenCode server versions accept a directory query parameter on session.create, which may be needed for the server to associate the session with the correct project.

Fix (in packages/smithy/src/providers/opencode/headless.ts, spawn method around line 196-202):

1. After calling client.session.create(), check result.error FIRST. If present, throw an error that includes the error details so the actual failure reason is visible:

   const result = await client.session.create({
     body: { title: options.initialPrompt?.slice(0, 100) || "Stoneforge Agent" },
   });
   if (result.error) {
     const detail = typeof result.error === "string" ? result.error : JSON.stringify(result.error);
     throw new Error("OpenCode session creation failed: " + detail);
   }
   if (!result.data?.id) {
     throw new Error("OpenCode session creation failed: no session ID in response");
