## Root Cause A: Polling creates new DOMRect every 500ms (Bugs 1 & 2)

**File:** `apps/smithy-web/src/components/onboarding/OnboardingTour.tsx`

The `updateTargetRect` callback (around line 397-411 equivalent in the worker branch) calls `el.getBoundingClientRect()` every 500ms via the polling interval. Each call returns a **new DOMRect object**, so even when the element hasn't moved, `setTargetRect(newRect)` triggers a state update because the object reference changed.

This flows into `TourTooltip`'s effect that depends on `targetRect`:

```ts
useEffect(() => {
    if (!targetRect || !tooltipRef.current) return;
    const tooltipHeight = tooltipRef.current.offsetHeight;
    const newCoords = calculateTooltipPosition(targetRect, tooltipHeight);
    setCoords(newCoords);
    requestAnimationFrame(() => { setIsVisible(true); });
    return () => { setIsVisible(false); };  // <-- resets visibility on every targetRect change
  }, [targetRect, step.id]);
```

Every 500ms: new DOMRect → `setTargetRect` → effect cleanup sets `isVisible(false)` → effect body sets `isVisible(true)` → **flickering**.

**Bug 2** (Back button closes tour) is a consequence: during the flicker, `coords` briefly becomes `null`, the tooltip moves to position (-9999, -9999) off-screen, and the user's click falls through to the backdrop's `onClick={onSkip}`, which closes the tour.

### Fix

In `updateTargetRect`, compare the new rect's values with the current rect before calling `setTargetRect`. Only update if position or size actually changed:

```ts
const updateTargetRect = useCallback(() => {
    if (!currentStepData) {
      setTargetRect(null);
      return;
    }

    const el = document.querySelector(
      `[data-testid="${currentStepData.targetTestId}"]`
    );
    if (el) {
      const newRect = el.getBoundingClientRect();
      setTargetRect((prev) => {
        if (
          prev &&
          prev.top === newRect.top &&
          prev.left === newRect.left &&
          prev.width === newRect.width &&
          prev.height === newRect.height
        ) {
          return prev; // No change — keep same reference
        }
        return newRect;
      });
    } else {
      setTargetRect(null);
    }
  }, [currentStepData]);
```

This prevents unnecessary re-renders when the element hasn't moved, eliminating the flickering and the consequent back-button-to-backdrop click-through.

