## Bug 3: Overlay disappears on some steps

### Root Cause

This is the same flickering issue from the earlier fix (el-x8n9ln) — the \`updateTargetRect\` callback may not have the DOMRect comparison fix properly applied, OR new steps have targets that temporarily don't exist during page transitions.

### Fix

Verify the DOMRect comparison fix is present in \`updateTargetRect\`:
\`\`\`typescript
setTargetRect((prev) => {
  if (prev && prev.top === newRect.top && prev.left === newRect.left &&
      prev.width === newRect.width && prev.height === newRect.height) {
    return prev;
  }
  return newRect;
});
\`\`\`

If it IS present, the overlay disappearing is because \`targetRect\` becomes null when the target element temporarily unmounts during navigation. The fix: when \`targetRect\` transitions from non-null to null AND \`isNavigating\` is false, keep the previous rect for a grace period (e.g., 500ms) before setting null. This prevents the flash:

\`\`\`typescript
const prevTargetRectRef = useRef<DOMRect | null>(null);

// In updateTargetRect:
if (el) {
  const newRect = el.getBoundingClientRect();
  prevTargetRectRef.current = newRect;
  setTargetRect(/* comparison logic */);
} else {
  // Don't immediately null out — keep previous rect briefly
  // The next poll will either find the element or the auto-advance will handle it
  // Only null out if we've been searching for a while
  if (!prevTargetRectRef.current) {
    setTargetRect(null);
  }
}
\`\`\`

Also check: the \`SpotlightOverlay\` returns null when targetRect is null. Consider showing the backdrop overlay WITHOUT the spotlight when targetRect is null (instead of removing everything):

\`\`\`typescript
// In SpotlightOverlay, instead of early return:
if (!targetRect) {
  return (
    <svg className="fixed inset-0 w-full h-full pointer-events-none" style={{ zIndex: 9998 }}>
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" fill="rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)" />
    </svg>
  );
}
\`\`\`

This ensures the dark overlay stays visible even when the target element is temporarily not found.

## Bug 4: Task detail step auto-advances to plans without user input

### Root Cause

The auto-advance timer fires after \`pollDuration + 500ms\` when the target element (\`task-detail-panel\`) is not found. The task detail panel takes time to render after the mock data is injected and the URL navigation happens. The 5.5-second timeout is sometimes too short, OR the panel never renders because mock data isn't being injected into the right query key (Bug 1).

### Fix

**Primary fix**: Fixing Bug 1 (injecting individual task query keys) will cause the detail panel to actually render, which means the target element WILL be found and the auto-advance timer will be cancelled.

**Secondary fix**: The auto-advance feature is too aggressive for steps that are programmatically opening panels. Add an opt-out field to TourStep:

\`\`\`typescript
// In TourStep interface:
/** If true, never auto-advance when target is not found (wait for user) */
noAutoAdvance?: boolean;
\`\`\`

Then in the auto-advance timer code in OnboardingTour.tsx:
\`\`\`typescript
if (!currentStepData?.noAutoAdvance) {
  autoAdvanceTimerRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
    const el = ...;
    if (!el) onNext();
  }, pollDuration + 500);
}
\`\`\`

Set \`noAutoAdvance: true\` on all detail panel steps: \`tasks-detail\`, \`plans-detail\`, \`documents-detail\`, \`messages-channel\`.

